      "title": "EXPE Q3 Earnings Call Highlights Higher Outlook & Q4 Caution",
      "summary": "Expedia Group raised its 2026 revenue guidance to $16.37-$16.43B following strong Q3 results with adjusted EBITDA rising 17% to $1.69B. The company reported robust B2B growth of 19% in bookings and 23% in revenues, though B2B margin pressure emerged. Q4 is expected to face headwinds from election-related demand softness, geopolitical disruptions, and tougher comparisons. Management emphasized AI expansion, consumer engagement improvements, and disciplined marketing as key drivers of margin expansion.",
